@* One lazily-loaded panel on a character/source page. It fetches on `load`, at the same moment as
   every other section on the page.

   IT USED TO BE STAGGERED, 500ms apart down the page, so that "one page view doesn't open six
   concurrent requests". That was caution rather than a measurement, and the measurement does not
   support it: the character page's six endpoints cost 127ms of query time BETWEEN THEM, and firing
   all six at once completes in 68ms — bounded by the slowest one, with every other endpoint as fast
   or faster than it was alone. The stagger was spending 3,000ms (the last section waited
   (5+1)x500ms before it even asked) to spread 127ms of work. 90 concurrent requests across three
   characters returned 90 200s with nothing empty or truncated.

   THIS IS NOT A LICENCE TO QUERY CONCURRENTLY DURING SSR — that rule is untouched and is the one
   that caused an outage. Each of these panels is its OWN HTMX request with its OWN request scope
   and its own DbContext, which is precisely why they may overlap. Sibling components loading data
   in a single render pass share one scoped DbContext and still must not. See CLAUDE.md.

   Two distinct waiting states, deliberately:
     - Deferred (rendered, request not yet away): a flat, unanimated block. No spinner and no
       pulse, because nothing is happening yet and a spinner would claim otherwise.
     - Loading (this section's request in flight): the spinner fades in. htmx puts htmx-request on
       the requesting element for exactly that span, and app.css keys .defer-spinner off it — so
       the state is driven by the real request, not a timer that could drift out of step with it.

   hx-swap="outerHTML" replaces this whole wrapper with the loaded panel, so the placeholder's
   frame and the panel's frame never both exist. *@
<div hx-get="@Url"
     hx-trigger="load"
     hx-swap="outerHTML"
     class="relative bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900 rounded-xl shadow-sm border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700 p-5">
    @if (ChildContent is not null)
    {
        @ChildContent
    }
    else
    {
        <div class="rounded bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800/60 @HeightClass"></div>
    }

    <div class="defer-spinner absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center pointer-events-none">
        <svg class="w-7 h-7 animate-spin text-amber-500 dark:text-amber-400" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle class="opacity-25" cx="12" cy="12" r="10" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="3"></circle>
            <path class="opacity-90" fill="currentColor" d="M4 12a8 8 0 018-8V0C5.373 0 0 5.373 0 12h4z"></path>
        </svg>
        <span class="sr-only">Loading</span>
    </div>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter] public required string Url { get; set; }

    /// Height of the default placeholder block, sized to the panel it stands in for so the
    /// page doesn't jump when the real content lands.
    [Parameter] public string HeightClass { get; set; } = "h-60";

    /// Optional bespoke placeholder (e.g. a header strip plus a chart area) when a single
    /// block would misrepresent the panel's shape.
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
